WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
- [Narrator] This is what
Nintendo originally was.

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.390
Yes, it was a playing card company.

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.857
And this is Nintendo today.

00:00:08.857 --> 00:00:10.710
- [Mario toy] "It's-a Me, Mario!"

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:11.610
- [Narrator] Consoles,

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:12.810
theme parks,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.250
even movies.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.180
So, what has driven
the $44 billion empire?

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.327
This is "The Economics of Nintendo."

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.990
Nintendo is different
from its competitor's,

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.610
Sony and Microsoft.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.820
Thanks, in part, to its low-cost hardware.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.540
Microsoft's Xbox makes no
profit on its hardware.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:36.570
- Consoles are actually sold
at a loss in the market.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.440
So when somebody goes

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.927
and they buy an Xbox at
their local retailer,

00:00:39.927 --> 00:00:42.150
we're subsidizing that purchase

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.747
somewhere between a hundred
and $200 with the expectation

00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:49.170
that we will recoup that
investment over time

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.330
through accessory sales and storefront.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.130
- [Narrator] And Sony only recently began

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.650
to make a profit on the PlayStation 5.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.990
Then there's Nintendo.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:01.560
- The technology is usually
five or six years behind

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:02.910
in terms of state of the art.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.580
But that means that
they're cheaper to produce

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.020
and that means that Nintendo

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:10.200
is much, much more profitable
on their hardware business.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.930
- [Narrator] About half of
Nintendo's profit in 2022

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.670
came from hardware sales.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.020
They've dominated the market

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.790
when it comes to handheld consoles.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.933
One of its big successes, the
Game Boy, launched in 1989.

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.860
- Nintendo was really early
to the party with handheld.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.660
They're kind of credited
with inventing the console,

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.670
although they were
probably third or fourth.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:34.440
- [Narrator] The Game Boy
had a longer battery life

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.940
compared to some of its competitors.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.570
Four shades of gray, nuanced
gameplay, and had Tetris,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:42.300
one of the top selling
video games of all time.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.920
Eventually, Nintendo's Game Boy

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.980
became the third most sold
console in the company's history,

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.280
selling 119 million units to date.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.990
The company continued to innovate,

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:54.060
releasing new hardware for its games,

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:58.080
from the GameCube, Nintendo DS, the Wii,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.880
and to its most recent success,

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.540
the Switch, with more than
122 million units sold.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.530
- [Sarah] You can play it at home

00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.450
like a console on your big screen TV,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.070
but you could pick it up
and take it on the go.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.440
And it becomes a handheld
device, and that's pretty novel.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.490
We haven't really seen anything

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.151
that's hybrid like that before.

00:02:13.151 --> 00:02:15.810
- [Narrator] Sales of the
Switch device and its games

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.260
accounted for about 94% of
Nintendo's sales revenue

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.450
in it's 2021 fiscal year.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:24.120
And today, it's the second
bestselling game console

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.380
in Nintendo's history,

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.410
and continues to be a driving
factor of its revenue.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.390
The success of Nintendo's consoles

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.340
is also due to its software.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.140
In other words, its games.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.830
In 2022, Nintendo had
19 first party titles

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.200
that sold over a million units each,

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.030
exclusive to its consoles.

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.983
- The difference between
the others and Nintendo

00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:48.904
is that Nintendo historically has produced

00:02:48.904 --> 00:02:53.490
about 50% of all the games
sold on its hardware system.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.570
And the other guys

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.350
are typically under 10% of the
games sold on their systems.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:01.195
So they make make a small
fraction of the software

00:03:01.195 --> 00:03:03.420
that's played on PlayStation and Xbox,

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.255
and Nintendo makes more than half.

00:03:05.255 --> 00:03:06.600
- [Narrator] Case in point,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.570
Animal Crossing: New Horizons,
release in April, 2020,

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.742
created higher demand for
the only console carrying it,

00:03:12.742 --> 00:03:13.890
the Switch.

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:15.205
- [Sarah] Nintendo makes games exclusively

00:03:15.205 --> 00:03:17.640
for the most part for its own devices.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.440
If you want to play a Nintendo game,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:22.184
like Legend of Zelda, you
need Nintendo hardware.

00:03:22.184 --> 00:03:24.600
- [Narrator] In fact,
Nintendo's first party games

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.000
generate over 70% of its sales.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.800
Its best sellers in 2022

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.937
were all Nintendo first party games.

00:03:30.937 --> 00:03:33.210
And the type of content Nintendo makes

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.370
is also different than its competitors.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.203
- [Sarah] Let's keep in mind,

00:03:36.203 --> 00:03:37.782
Nintendo characters are very cute.

00:03:37.782 --> 00:03:40.086
- [Mario toy] "It's-a Me, Mario!"

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:41.640
- [Sarah] Nintendo is known

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:44.010
for making family friendly
games for the most part,

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:46.140
so it appeals to a different crowd

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.940
than some of the other publishers.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:50.700
You won't see blood or
gore, or foul language.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.290
But even Nintendo a couple years ago

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.030
dabbled into the shooter genre.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:55.380
When we think of shooters, right,

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.133
we think of Call of Duty, Fortnite.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:00.720
They take a very family
friendly approach with Splatoon.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.640
It's a shooter, but you're
shooting paintballs.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.320
- [Narrator] The company's next iteration,

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.230
bringing these family friendly
characters to a larger arena

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.810
and building another generation of fans.

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:11.340
In February, 2023,

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:14.940
Nintendo opened its first
theme park outside of Japan.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:18.060
And in April, it's releasing
a Super Mario Brothers movie

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.260
starring Chris Pratt.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.330
- It's-a Me, Mario.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.200
- That's smart,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.770
because that's gonna
expose the Nintendo brand

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:27.570
to hundreds of millions of people

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.340
who haven't ever owned a Switch.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:33.750
I don't think that Nintendo
is necessarily worried about

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.460
whether somebody who
goes to the theme park

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.880
will buy a Nintendo console or buy a game,

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.680
but they want those people

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.990
to be aware of the Nintendo brands,

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:45.780
and they want them to know who
Mario is, and who Zelda is,

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.250
and who Yoshi is, and who Pickmin is.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.059
- It is risky to start a new franchise,

00:04:50.059 --> 00:04:52.810
and sometimes new properties
just don't resonate,

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.620
but they have plenty, a very deep library,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.840
and they've stuck with
that for the most part,

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.700
and iterated on it and modernized it.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.440
We'll probably be playing Legends of Zelda

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.120
for another 20, 30 years.

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.268
Mario is probably not going anywhere.

00:05:05.268 --> 00:05:07.440
You know, he's just gonna live forever,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.910
and keep that mustache,

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.467
and keep everyone happy
for many years to come.

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:14.050
(upbeat music)

